findings.claim:
Under 97.301(a), Region 2, a Technician may use 420-450, 902-928, 1240-1300, 2300-2310, 2390-2450 and 5650-5925 MHz, at the minimum power necessary and no more than 1.5 kW PEP (97.313). The FCC fee has been $35 since 19 April 2022; upgrades carry no fee. Conditions:
- station ID at least every 10 minutes and no unidentified signals (97.119);
- no messages encoded to obscure their meaning, and no pecuniary interest (97.113(a)(4) and (a)(3));
- RF-exposure compliance (97.13(c));
- no transmitting in 420-430 MHz north of Line A, and protect other nations' radionavigation-satellite (GNSS) services at 23 cm (97.303).
The 9 cm band is effectively gone: 3.45-3.5 GHz ended on 14 April 2022, 3.3-3.45 GHz continues only pending FCC action, and the current 97.301 table no longer lists it.
